"**FBI Ten\u2013Most\u2011Wanted fugitives added in 2000\u202for\u202f2001 who were *convicted of murder within ten years of their placement on the list***\n\n| # | Name | Date added to the Ten\u2011Most\u2011Wanted list | Murder conviction (year) | Source |\n|---|------|----------------------------------------|---------------------------|--------|\n| 459 | **Jesse\u202fJames\u202fCaston** | 19\u202fAug\u202f2000 | Second\u2011degree murder of Sharon\u202fMcIntyre (pleaded guilty 2004; sentenced to life) | \u30106\u2020L4-L9\u3011 |\n| 461 | **Aurlieas\u202fDame\u202fMcClarty** | 24\u202fFeb\u202f2001 | Two counts of first\u2011degree murder (convicted 7\u202fMay\u202f2008; sentenced to life) | \u30107\u2020L0-L8\u3011 |\n\n### Why only these two?\n\n- **Eric Franklin Rosser** (460) was convicted of child\u2011pornography offenses, not murder.  \n- **Hopeton Eric Brown** (462) was killed in 2004; no conviction.  \n- **Maghfoor Mansoor** (463), **Francis William Murphy** (464), **Dwight Bowen** (465), **Nikolay Soltys** (466), and **Clayton Lee Waagner** (467) were apprehended without being charged with murder (or were not convicted of murder).  \n\nThus, the only FBI Ten\u2011Most\u2011Wanted fugitives added in 2000 or 2001 who met the criterion \u201cconvicted of murder within ten years after placement\u201d are **Jesse\u202fJames\u202fCaston** and **Aurlieas\u202fDame\u202fMcClarty**."